# Read by the `ignore` crate (and by ripgrep/fd), NOT by git — which is exactly the point.
#
# Conformance fixture corpora are deliberately-flawed test data: checked into git and
# exercised by the conformance gate's own `cargo test` run, but excluded from kndo's
# self-check of its own repository — analyzing them would report every flaw they were
# written to contain. An entry in .gitignore would also govern `git add` and silently
# skip a newly added fixture; `.ignore` states the exclusion once and means only that.
**/tests/fixtures/

# Frozen experiment records (the M-1 fingerprint spike): evidence for the decision they
# measured, not product code.
/spikes/

# Oracle output and corpus measurements: JSON captured from real runs, not code.
/oracle/
/corpus-findings/

# Third-party source vendored verbatim for one build-flag fix (its README records the
# one deviation): not the code under judgment, and its manifest is not ours to align.
/vendor/
